#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549027 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105872 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7656d23-06c9-5d22-b62a-3636bca66ab6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Base or the Height of a Triangle Given Its Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ed3ec42-7887-59f4-8607-49a2c72ca3d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49\\,cm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548449} {:answer/id #uuid "498f62c4-d10e-5980-af7b-cf193748dc55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\,cm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548494} {:answer/id #uuid "68718dec-ecd8-5ae5-a90a-23ccd4586c90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,cm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548552} {:answer/id #uuid "897c0883-8ea7-5679-b872-375f1438d23b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,cm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548619} {:answer/id #uuid "b854d192-b8ff-551c-8ab1-aef38e4dfe2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\,cm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "897c0883-8ea7-5679-b872-375f1438d23b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,cm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548619} :answer-field/id #uuid "8da7771e-63f1-5e10-be3c-1af25ccedf2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548930}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8d086598-d0f7-52ac-bba9-a6017b092d64" :question/math-academy-id "q-21051" :question/problem "![](images/c8/c85e6ee974a59d956367634fdd1d57b65e9d42a980fe1750886527b173f05d32.png)\n\nFind $BM$ given that the area of $△ACB$ is $49\\,{cm}^{2},$ $AM=5\\,cm,$ and $MC=9\\,cm.$\n\n(Figure not drawn to scale)" :question/worked-solution "The area of the triangle is defined as \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n where $b$ is the base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the height is $h=BM,$ and the corresponding base is \n\n$$\nb=AM+MC=14\\,cm.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the formula for the area, we can solve for the height as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\ 49 & =\\frac{14\\cdot h}{2} \\\\ 98 & =14\\cdot h \\\\ h & =\\frac{98}{14} \\\\ h & =7\\,cm\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $BM=7\\,\\text{cm}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549052 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105871 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6445834c-7788-5427-a72c-30b06cc8e6ab" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of an Isosceles Right Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "417abf8e-a35f-5695-b467-ef4d6b12c3f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548479} {:answer/id #uuid "5cfd8bf4-6acb-5b60-99c2-c71861b1536a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548526} {:answer/id #uuid "a449dec1-300a-5c71-8723-ab8f3583b39a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548678} {:answer/id #uuid "b32a6fda-8006-5e0b-bc5e-adba5d208d71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548714} {:answer/id #uuid "e8a23dd6-a819-573e-923b-b6ed5c0e58fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "417abf8e-a35f-5695-b467-ef4d6b12c3f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548479} :answer-field/id #uuid "20a135df-b545-5cd9-8ae5-be9b531bfe60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548881}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d45bf6d6-3e38-52ed-a276-f99fe5dd268f" :question/math-academy-id "q-87851" :question/problem "![](images/67/678c719915b0d27c1378548267123cfbac3f13f13ee0a05fd6dacd85164911f6.png)\n\nWhat is the area of the right triangle $ABC$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Since $m∠A=m∠C={45}^{∘}$ and $AB=BC,$ we have an isosceles right triangle. \n\n![](images/4d/4d340b37161cb3f970ba588fa15a21b3a35ee376c5766e92d6c48358d4ed003e.png)\n\nTherefore, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {5}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 25 \\\\  & =12.5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354604 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105871 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6445834c-7788-5427-a72c-30b06cc8e6ab" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of an Isosceles Right Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2db54839-6a5b-5b75-9ac0-2fe3487ce8c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "800" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351989} {:answer/id #uuid "43e30190-4e81-5fda-b3a5-079b052411c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352191} {:answer/id #uuid "43f1421d-10d0-5af6-8262-60e55e5615e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352192} {:answer/id #uuid "50c4006c-d6f4-5cb3-977c-4236359a9cc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "200" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352294} {:answer/id #uuid "7d349513-c9f4-5a55-81fa-6b46f8d0946e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "400" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352666}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50c4006c-d6f4-5cb3-977c-4236359a9cc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "200" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352294} :answer-field/id #uuid "23513061-aa39-51dd-a874-2807ff166615" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353872}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e4dded3-cef3-55b9-ba8c-e50ddf3e7619" :question/math-academy-id "q-87853" :question/problem "![](images/16/1616f8d921cbdaf1a5654354292e261b0941e5dbfcee16ae620c8a1cf3e92135.png)\n\nWhat is the area of the right triangle $ABC$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Since $m∠A=m∠C={45}^{∘}$ and $AB=BC,$ we have an isosceles right  triangle. \n\n![](images/3f/3f9a52834fe76f1560beec8580dbd91076a9f7c6ef980f410aa5bfe7da162c9c.png)\n\nTherefore, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {20}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 400 \\\\  & =200.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
